  "name": "Fanbai (Han Chinese Buddhist liturgical chant)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Liturgical chant of Han Chinese Buddhist monasteries, sung by the assembled monks or nuns at the morning and evening services and in larger rites, with temples such as Kaiyuan Temple in Quanzhou documented on record. A precentor sets the pitch and the assembly answers in unison, the recitation paced by the muyu wooden fish and the qing bowl-bell (the temple-bells card stands in for the qing), with small hand cymbals in some rites.",
